ainst the tool's own contract, and that a newly declared int-typed timestamp field must carry an `int | str` annotation.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Fix shape: 'emit an integer outside the JS-safe range as its exact decimal string, so int(wire_value) == stored_value'","ACs cover naming the field, no-error returns, a regression test, and live validation — but none require the advertised outputSchema/JSON-schema field type to be widened to accept a string","The MCP structured-output contract is LLM/tool-consumed (TicketStateOut -> FastMCP outputSchema), so a wire-type-vs-declared-type divergence is a structural gap in that contract","ABSENCE: no AC or verification method addresses the type declared for these fields in the tool's outputSchema"],"finding":"The plan's fix widens the emitted wire type of timestamp fields (created_at/updated_at, comments[].timestamp, signed_at) from JSON number to JSON string, but no acceptance criterion requires the tool's advertised structured-output contract (the FastMCP outputSchema, backed by ticket_state.schema.json / common.schema.json / *_result.schema.json) to accept the string form. A strict MCP client that validates structuredContent against the advertised 'integer'-typed schema would reject the string wire value the fix now emits.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fab2a3867966b0d83","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria + 'Fix shape' section","norm_id":"n09970d3cdefd4c93","priority":0.875,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An MCP client (or FastMCP's own output_model.model_validate re-check) validates the tool's structuredContent against an outputSchema that still declares created_at/updated_at as 'integer', and rejects the string wire value the fix emits","A future declared int-typed timestamp field is re-coerced back to a bare number by model_validate, silently reintroducing the bug"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'The outputSchema advertised for list_tickets/ready_tickets/show_ticket (and the mirrored ticket_state/common/*_result schema files) declares created_at/updated_at/comments[].timestamp/signed_at as type [\"integer\",\"string\"], so the string wire form validates against the tool contract. Verify: a test asserts the advertised schema accepts a string value for these fields, and the drift gate covers a declared int-typed timestamp field requiring an int|str annotation.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan root cause: 'plain JSON.parse → the value silently truncates (no error)' vs 'a lossless parser (GitHub Copilot CLI ...) → yields a BigInt ... throws'","The AC phrasing 'through a JS client ... with no BigInt serialization error' is satisfied by ANY plain-JSON.parse client regardless of whether the fix shipped, because such a client never throws"],"finding":"The LIVE VALIDATION acceptance criteria do not pin that the validating JS client must be one whose LOSSLESS parse would have surfaced the original BigInt error; a plain-JSON.parse client would pass 'no BigInt serialization error' even against the still-broken build (it silently truncates rather than throwing).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f52158c107cd2749c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria → LIVE VALIDATION → 'returns through a JS client ... with no BigInt serialization error'","norm_id":"ndcf8b8ba3df87712","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Amend the two live-validation criteria to name the client (or class of client) whose lossless parse reproduced the original TypeError, and require the recorded response to show the timestamp value round-trips exactly (int(wire)==stored) rather than only 'no error'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan requires: 'list_tickets ... returns through a JS client against that deployed endpoint'","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:347-351 sets REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL / REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL to https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp — the endpoint enforces OAuth","docs/mcp-auth.md and docs/mcp-client-setup.md:86 show the copilot client is configured with an auth token; infra/terraform/auth/edge-gate is a live auth gate","T3 checklist (c): auth/HTTPS preconditions stated — HTTPS is (the URL), auth is absent"],"finding":"The LIVE VALIDATION section requires reaching the deployed https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp endpoint through a JS client but states no auth/token precondition, though that endpoint is behind OAuth/SSO.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32524a620eda6533","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria → LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE","norm_id":"n773b9f662c9737aa","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add to the LIVE VALIDATION preamble the auth requirement: the JS client must present the OAuth bearer/token that docs/mcp-client-setup.md configures (per REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL), and name how the validator obtains it.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Fix shape: 'so int(wire_value) == stored_value with no rounding'","Root cause: 'the value silently truncates (no error): stored 1787856371950409998 reads back as 1787856371950410000'","AC: 'returns a ticket list with no serialization error. Verify: the tool call returns a well-formed result.'"],"finding":"No acceptance criterion verifies that the timestamp value round-trips exactly (int(wire_value) == stored_value with no rounding). The ACs only check 'no serialization error', but the plan's own root cause identifies silent truncation (1787856371950409998 -> 1787856371950410000) as the more dangerous failure mode for plain-JSON.parse clients. A fix that stringifies could pass every 'no error' AC while still not being verified to preserve the exact value.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe31cfc7168786bea","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria / regression test AC","norm_id":"n88d468e32d4db1bc","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the regression test AC, assert the exact-value contract: parse the wire timestamp, int()-convert, and assert equality with the stored time_ns value (e.g. the 19-digit integer is preserved exactly).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'More ride in raw list[dict] fields: comments[].timestamp, attestations.<kind>.signed_at, signature.signed_at.'","'show_ticket 2' integers measured","ACs cover only list_tickets and ready_tickets"],"finding":"The root cause names show_ticket (2 integers) and nested raw list[dict] fields (comments[].timestamp, attestations.<kind>.signed_at, signature.signed_at) as carriers of the hazard, but no acceptance criterion exercises show_ticket or a ticket that actually contains comments/attestations/signature. The fix is described as applying 'at the MCP tool-return seam only' generically, yet the ACs only exercise list_tickets and ready_tickets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbe212b7481ba9d61","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause 'The changeable artifacts' / Acceptance criteria","norm_id":"nd67ed6f35645917a","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend the regression test to include a ticket with at least one comment and an attestation/signature, and assert those nested signed_at/timestamp values also round-trip exactly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the test exists, fails when the guard is disabled, and passes with it enabled'","Root cause: 'stored 1787856371950409998 reads back as 1787856371950410000. This is why the tool \"worked\" from Claude Code while quietly corrupting data.'","Fix shape: 'int(wire_value) == stored_value with no rounding'"],"finding":"The regression-test acceptance criterion asserts only 'no serialization error' / 'returns a ticket list', not that the out-of-range timestamp survives losslessly (int(wire_value) == stored_value). A fix that emits a lossy/truncated value — or a test that snapshots current output — could pass this criterion while silently corrupting data, which is the exact silent-truncation failure mode the root-cause section documents for plain JSON.parse clients.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f66e481cb17e6934d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — 'An MCP-layer regression test exercises list_tickets... fails when the guard is disabled'","norm_id":"n905408cc123f0f84","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add to the test AC: the test must parse the emitted string field and assert equality with the original 19-digit stored integer, covering a value strictly greater than 2**53-1.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py — list_tickets / show_ticket / ready_tickets return those models.'","Plan: 'Tools whose models carry no ticket timestamps (search, summary, ticket_deps, explain_criterion, grounding_info) emit 0 and do not fail — a split that predicts exactly which tools break.'","src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:377-382: `def recent_session_logs(limit: int = 5) -> list[TicketStateOut]: ... return [TicketStateOut.model_validate(t) for t in rebar.recent_session_logs(limit=limit)]` — a fourth TicketStateOut-returning tool the plan's 'exactly which tools break' split omits."],"finding":"The inventory of tools that emit ticket timestamps via `TicketStateOut` is incomplete: it names `list_tickets` / `show_ticket` / `ready_tickets` and claims to 'predict exactly which tools break', but `recent_session_logs` is a fourth call site of `TicketStateOut` (`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:377`, returning `list[TicketStateOut]` from `rebar.recent_session_logs`) that passes the same undeclared `created_at`/`updated_at` `time.time_ns()` integers through the identical seam and would break identically.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f75dcea80c098ab96","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause -> 'src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py -- list_tickets / show_ticket / ready_tickets return those models' and 'a split that predicts exactly which tools break'","norm_id":"nd57961996878d316","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the root-cause 'which tools break' list and the fix scope, include recent_session_logs alongside list_tickets/show_ticket/ready_tickets (all four return TicketStateOut), and either extend an AC to cover it or state why its lower call frequency doesn't need one.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the LIVE VALIDATION preconditions: the specific JS client used to hit `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` and any auth/access requirement (public, bearer token, or network/VPN) needed to reach that deployed endpoint.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3257,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Observed against the DEPLOYED server at https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp'","Plan quote: 'returns through a JS client against that deployed endpoint' — the JS client is unnamed and its availability in the validating environment is unstated","HTTPS is satisfied (the URL is https), but no auth/access precondition is stated for the deployed endpoint","ANTI-FP: feasibility itself is evidenced — the original bug report was produced by such a client (GitHub Copilot CLI), so this is a precondition-completeness gap, not a capability gap"],"finding":"The LIVE VALIDATION section depends on reaching the deployed MCP endpoint `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` through a 'JS client', but states no authentication/access precondition for that endpoint (public vs token/VPN-gated) and names no specific JS client tool to run the call.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa10cd8c1e4d9cb4a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria → LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE","norm_id":"n22973055d0340be3","priority":0.5743,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A validator on a network without access to rebar.solutions.navateam.com, or lacking a required auth token, cannot execute the REQUIRED-TO-CLOSE checks and cannot tell whether the failure is the bug, an auth wall, or a network wall"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the compatibility posture for the number→string wire change: enumerate which fields flip type, note that this breaks any client reading them as numbers, and record an explicit rollback/back-out path (or justify the break as strictly-better than the current corruption).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.635,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'emit an integer outside the JS-safe range as its exact decimal string'","'plain JSON.parse → the value silently truncates ... This is why the tool \"worked\" from Claude Code'","No section addresses how clients that do arithmetic/`typeof number` on created_at/updated_at behave after the type flips to string; no rollback path is stated."],"finding":"The fix changes the wire representation of timestamp fields from a JSON number to a JSON string (for out-of-range values), which is an interface/data-shape change consumed by MCP clients, but the plan provides no expand-contract sequence, no rollback/back-out plan, and no analysis of clients that currently read these fields as numbers (e.g. the Claude Code client the plan says was silently truncating them).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f44a3b88c427a0d08","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause → 'Fix shape'","norm_id":"n70cbe20e6bcf74c7","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An existing MCP client parses created_at as a number and performs date arithmetic; after the fix it receives a string and the arithmetic breaks or NaNs.","A rollback is needed because a downstream consumer regressed; the plan has no back-out mechanism documented."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a short 'Compatibility & rollback' note: the change flips out-of-range int timestamps to decimal strings only at the MCP return seam; document that JS clients must parse these as BigInt/string, confirm no in-repo consumer relies on the numeric type, and state the back-out (revert the serializer shim) since the prior behavior was either an error or silent corruption.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.635,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'emit an integer outside the JS-safe range as its exact decimal string, so int(wire_value) == stored_value'","'CLI --output json and the Python library are unchanged' (MCP consumers not addressed)"],"finding":"The fix changes the JSON wire TYPE of timestamp fields from number to string for MCP consumers (so clients must int()-parse), which is a consumer-facing contract change for any MCP JS client that currently reads these as numbers. The plan states CLI --output json and the Python library are unchanged, but does not explicitly acknowledge the number->string change as a breaking-shape change for MCP consumers, nor a rollback/back-out path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc4a972986e7c542e","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause 'Fix shape'","norm_id":"nbe1d117ac1eb40c9","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence noting the MCP seam changes affected timestamps to decimal strings, that this supersedes the previously-corrupting numeric emission, and describe how to revert (single-seam guard is toggleable/removable).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the new MCP-return-seam JS-safe-integer invariant durably (a comment at the serialization seam and/or AGENTS.md note) so future large-int fields inherit the rule, mirroring how the event path is pinned.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The MCP surface never generalized that rule. This bug is that missing generalization'","'src/rebar/_store/canonical.py and _store/hlc.py keep jq out of the event path because it \"parses as float64 and rounds\", pinned by tests/unit/test_canonical.py'","The ACs add one regression test but do not require documenting the new MCP-seam serialization invariant so it is not re-lost the next time a model adds a large-int field."],"finding":"The plan introduces a new serialization rule at the MCP tool-return seam that generalizes the existing event-path rule, but does not state where the decision is captured (ADR/AGENTS.md/comment) beyond the single regression test, whereas the cited precedent is pinned by both code comments and tests/unit/test_canonical.py.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f52931bb230b17234","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"locati